      "message": "what about calling common_intel_x86_handle_rsmrst here?\n\nWe could remove the enum power_state state parameter (since it is unused in that function) and make a note that is could be called in either interrupt or task context.\n\nThen in common_86x if CONFIG_CHIPSET_X8^_RMSRST_ISR_PASS is defined, we skip the call to common_intel_x86_handle_rsmrst.\n\nWhat are you thoughts?\n\n(we would also need to remove the print from common_intel_x86_handle_rsmrst)\n\n\n----\n\n\nFor boards that define both CONFIG_CHIPSET_X86_RSMRST_ISR_PASS and CONFIG_BOARD_HAS_BEFORE_RSMRST right now, the board_before_rmsrst(0) would never get called.",
